	(text "Decoupling: each cap is drawn on the U5 pin (or VDD_RF pin pair) it serves; place it at that pin on the\nboard. C55 sits at Y3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0bf50fc5-894f-4647-8eab-ffde8c695e05")
	)
	(text "Y3: Epson TG2520SMN 26 MHz, +/-0.5 ppm, fed by the\nPX100's own TCXO LDO (pin 3). Its long side is the\ng-sensitive X axis (0.4 ppb/g typ): keep it across the\nthrust axis (board x). C56 is a 0 ohm link: the TCXO drives TCXO_I\ndirectly, as in SkyTraq's reference (refit 1 nF if the clock fails).\nY5: 32.768 kHz, no load capacitors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "14581029-f349-4db3-bcdf-803eaacb8af9")
	)
	(text "J9: three pogo landing pads, 2.54 mm apart, no part fitted. Pad 1 (the squared one) GND,\npad 2 PX100 TXD (to the bridge's RX), pad 3 PX100 RXD (from the bridge's TX).\nU32 (GPIO40) drives RXD too, but through R149 (1 k), so a bridge on pad 3 wins\nwith the flight computer running. On the board, R149 sits between U32 and the pad."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 220.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2de9f1ba-3c8d-5da8-9b5d-13e83bc02fb2")
	)
	(text "AE1: Taoglas GVLB258.A, a passive single-feed stacked L1/L5 ceramic patch, 25 x 25 x 8.12 mm (wider than the\nboard). Passive, so no antenna bias: U5 pin 9 (ANT_BIAS) is left open. Taoglas tunes it on a 70 x 70 mm\nground plane; the Beetle's is far smaller, so expect it to detune and check it on the rig.\nD5 clamps ESD at the feed; C7 is the DC block into the diplexer."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2eba5da2-445b-4a47-b60c-a952286805ea")
	)
	(text "915 MHz trap for the board's own LoRa transmitter (902-928 MHz):\nL14 + C159 short the line to ground at 915 MHz (about 20 dB);\nC160 cancels what they leave at 1176 MHz.\nPlace all three at the diplexer side of C69, each ground with its own via."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "300d23e8-e026-50b7-9028-a4662b87fb91")
	)
	(text "Reset RC (R7/C62), BOOT_SEL high = boot from flash (R14), UART idle-high pull-ups (R20/R24)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "31f81dca-1a5a-4967-a85c-d743d4a78ee7")
	)
	(text "Core: R6 5.1 ohm into the on-chip DC/DC, L8 2.2 uH to V_CORE, D15 Schottky clamp (DS p12)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "41563943-9bef-46fe-99da-649287b3b1b7")
	)
	(text "The exposed pad (41) is the chip's ONLY ground: give it a solid, short path to the ground layers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 198.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "479c750c-7263-436f-8e32-97279ed9c440")
	)
	(text "at U13 pin 6\n100 pF first"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "675b6033-aef4-4f71-af93-d680d7a24419")
	)
	(text "Antenna match (pi network): C157 - C7 - C158.\nC157 and C158 are tuning positions, left unfitted.\nTheir values come from tuning the patch on this board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 91.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "88315aac-cf9e-50ca-8b2e-b6e6dd0026d3")
	)
	(text "U12: C63 470 pF + L12 7.5 nH per the AT2659S data sheet; RFOUT is matched on chip, C67 blocks DC.\nU13: C69 100 pF + L13 9.1 nH per the ATR2652S data sheet's 1150-1300 MHz circuit (22.5 dB, 0.75 dB noise figure);\nRFOUT needs no match, C72 100 pF blocks DC. Pin 5 (EN) is its enable, high = on, tied to V_LNA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8f38059f-ff81-45cb-bf05-b3ff2e9dbef2")
	)
	(text "LNA supply: V_MCU_SWTCH -> R25 (10 ohm) -> V_LNA rail -> U12 pin 6 VDD (and pin 5 SHDN) and U13 pin 6 VDD (and pin 5 EN).\nC70 (100 pF) and C71 go at U12 pin 6; C64 (100 pF) and C66 go at U13 pin 6: the 100 pF first, within 2 mm, each with its own ground via.\nC75 sits by R25. U12 is drawn flipped so both LNA supply pins face the rail. LNA current = V(V_MCU_SWTCH - V_LNA) / 10 ohm, about 9 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9ada2442-96ec-4c2b-8ff5-8967813c0e02")
	)
	(text "RF chain: AE1 GVLB258.A passive L1/L5 patch -> D5 ESD -> C7 (pi match with C157/C158) -> L1/L5 diplexer FL1 -> one LNA per band (U12 AT2659S on L1; U13 ATR2652S on L5, behind a 915 MHz trap)\n-> band SAW -> SkyTraq L-match -> PX100. From the gnss-px100-18mm-hv V2 carrier's RF page, less its antenna bias, active-antenna bypass, PPS LED (the Sensors sheet has one),\ntest pads, header and supply. The L5 amplifier, its trap and the antenna match pads are the Beetle's own."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9dcb4405-c68b-4301-afc8-f01954625d41")
	)
	(text "PX100-5C-01A (SkyTraq PX100 DS p12 reference; pin wiring as on the TinkerNav PX100 V2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c508a73a-2d71-4653-98b6-17739e501490")
	)
	(text "FL2 (L1) and FL3 (L5, the TA2471A of SkyTraq's reference) are 50 ohm with no matching.\nC14 + L2 and C15 4 pF + L7 are SkyTraq's input matches into the PX100.\nC68 and C74 keep DC off the SAWs if pins 40 and 37 carry a bias (the carrier's 2026-10-27 review, V2 item 5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 228.6 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d4226d66-473a-4491-946d-2812bf2ccf5b")
	)
	(text "at U12 pin 6\n100 pF first"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 60.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "e340770e-77e4-4744-893f-99a0a1d39f64")
	)
	(text "TP1 (RSTN) and TP2 (BOOT_SEL) are the PX100's recovery pads. R14 holds BOOT_SEL\nhigh = boot from flash; pull it low through a reset to boot without the flash image."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.26 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e9cee976-7f03-42a1-addf-2663945a9693")
	)
	(text "SH1: Laird BMI-S-102, a one-piece shield (16.5 x 16.5 x 3.6 mm, vented top) on the\nland pattern of the BMI-S-202-F frame it replaces. It does not open: solder it\nafter inspection and the first sky test; any rework under it means taking it off.\nThe PX100's UART stays reachable on the pogo pads J9."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 312.42 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "efca91f9-590a-4002-b7fd-5572cf778151")
	)
	(text "R149: 1 k in series, so a\nUSB bridge on J9 pad 3 can\noverride U32 (GPIO40)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f658b47f-1c02-5874-bd66-42690fd03aa1")
	)
	(text "Decoupling is drawn at the pin it serves; place it at that pin.\nVDD_RF: C60 pin 39, C78 pin 38, C57 pin 34, C79 pin 35, C58 pin 1, C80 pin 2.\nVDD11 net: C39 at pin 16, C38 at pin 23 (the carrier's V1 had both by pin 23). C77 at pin 14."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.41 214.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fede9c9e-19f0-4d2c-8eb0-5369eaa2503d")
	)
